{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 49, :comments ["<b>As the eagle swoops.</b> Suddenly, and his way prospers, and his horses are swift." "<b>You will not understand his language.</b> You will not recognize his tongue — and so ״תִּשְׁמַע חֲלוֹם לִפְתֹּר אֹתוֹ״ (Genesis 41), and so ״כִּי שֹׁמֵעַ יוֹסֵף״ (ibid. 42); אינטינדד׳רי בְּלַעַ״ז."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {1 "The la'az אינטינדד׳רי is Old French entendre, 'to understand'; Rashi uses it to gloss שמע in the sense of 'comprehend'."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:41.989836461Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}